LEGAL BASIS:

Under Article 17 of the GDPR, I have the right to obtain the erasure of personal data concerning me without undue delay where:
- The personal data is no longer necessary for the purposes for which it was collected
- I withdraw my consent and there is no other legal ground for the processing
- I object to the processing and there are no overriding legitimate grounds
- The personal data has been unlawfully processed

Under Article 21 of the GDPR, I also object to the processing of my personal data for direct marketing purposes, including profiling to the extent related to such direct marketing. This right is absolute and cannot be refused.

REQUEST:
1. Delete all personal information you hold about me from your databases
2. Remove my information from any data broker networks or partner sharing arrangements
3. Communicate this erasure request to any recipients to whom you have disclosed my personal data (Article 19 GDPR)
4. Confirm the deletion in writing within one month as required by Article 12 of the GDPR

Please note that under Article 12 of the GDPR, you are required to respond to this request without undue delay and within one month. This period may be extended by two further months for complex requests, but you must inform me of such an extension within the first month.

Failure to comply may result in a complaint to the relevant supervisory authority under Article 77 of the GDPR, and/or legal proceedings under Article 79 of the GDPR.

If you require any additional information to verify my identity or locate my records, please contact me at {{.Email}}.

Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter.

Sincerely,
